  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "The oblique case is used with postpositions, and in other special situations.\n\nDirect    Oblique     Examples\n\nमैं       मुझ         मुझसे    (than I / from me)   मुझ पर   (on me)   मेरा (my)\nयह       इस          इससे     (than him/her)         इसमें    (in it / in this)  इसका (his/her/its)\nये       इन          इनसे     (than he/than they)    इनमें    (in him/in them)   इनका (his/her/their)\nवह       उस          उससे     (than she/from him)    उसपर    (on it)      उसका (his/her/its)\nवे       उन          उनसे     (than he/than they)    उनमें    (among them)   उनका (his/her/their)\nआप      आप         आपसे     (than you/from you)    आपमें    (among you)   आपका (your)\nहम       हम          हमसे     (from us/than we)      हममें    (among us)   हमारा (our)\n\nThese are only some of the possible meanings."
    }
